  <prompt>
    Ship the workspace-intelligence PRECURSORS only (FR-B-13): next-step chips on OutcomeCards (from the Binding's declared transitions, per FR-A1-06) + record-scope memory items (FR-B-01). Full goal-tracking is a NAMED DEFERRAL — do NOT build a goal-tracking subsystem here. These are the two seams a future goal-tracking project consumes.
  </prompt>

  <role>Senior full-stack developer fluent in the OutcomeCard chip model (SpaarkeAi + AI.Widgets) and the generalized record memory service.</role>

  <goal>
    Next-step chips appear on OutcomeCards, sourced from the Binding's declared transitions (not model invention), and record-scope memory items are captured as workspace-intelligence precursors. No goal-tracking subsystem, state machine, or new Dataverse tables are introduced — the two precursors are the extent of in-scope work, shaped so a future goal-tracking project can consume them.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/plan.md</file>
